===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|implācāble||immitigable, unappeasable}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=implācāble|pos=adj|id=MED22196|accessdate=4 December 2018}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|implacable||harsh, unrelenting; implacable}} (modern {{cog|fr|implacable}}), from {{der|en|la|implācābilis||unappeasable, implacable; irreconcilable}}, from {{m|la|im-}} (variant of {{m|la|in-|pos=''prefix meaning ‘not’''}}) + {{m|la|plācābilis||placable; appeasing, moderating, pacifying, propitiating; acceptable}} (from {{m|la|plācō||to assuage, pacify, placate; to appease; to reconcile}} + {{m|la|-bilis|pos=''suffix forming adjectives indicating a capacity or worth of being acted upon''}}).<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=92421|date=1899|nodot=yes}}; {{R:Lexico}}</ref>

